# Walkthrough: Cosma Cleanup and Relocation

I have successfully removed the Cosma installation traces from the root of your Obsidian vault to resolve the graph configuration issues.

## Changes Made

- **Relocated Configuration**: Moved [cosma.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma.yml), [config.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/config.yml), [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/package.json), and [package-lock.json](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/package-lock.json) to a new folder: [cosma_workspace/](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace).
- **Cleaned Root**: Deleted `node_modules` and moved the `export/` folder to the workspace.
- **Updated Config**: Modified [cosma.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace/cosma.yml) to point to `../` so it can still analyze your vault files from its new location.

## Verification Results

- [x] **Root Clean**: The root of `Ecosistema_Fintech_Global` no longer contains Cosma files.
- [x] **Relocation Verified**: Files are safely stored in `cosma_workspace/`.
- [x] **Graph State**: Obsidian should no longer try to index or show these configuration files in your graph.

